+# Team page
+
+## Problem
+Signed-in users have nowhere to see who is on their team or to invite someone new.
+
+## Appetite
+Small batch (1–2 days).
+
+## Solution
+- `/team`, signed-in only, linked from the main navigation.
+- Member list: name, email, role (owner, admin, member), status (active, invited) as a coloured badge.
+- Search box above the list filters by name or email as the user types (fragment swap, no reload).
+- "Invite member" form (name, email, role): name required, email valid and not already on the team.
+  Errors render next to their fields and keep what was typed; success adds an invited member to
+  the list and resets the form, no reload.
+- States: empty team prompts an invite; a search with no matches says so and names the query.
+
+## Rabbit Holes
+- Persistence: members live in an in-memory store inside the feature, seeded with three members.
+  A restart resets it; that is accepted for this batch.
+
+## No-Gos
+- Database or Prisma schema changes.
+- Sending invitation emails, accepting invites, removing members, editing roles.
